{"name":"Yellow Submarine","hex":"#ffff14","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"yellow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of sunflower petals and lemons; the color obtained by mixing green and red light, or by subtracting blue from white light; the color evoked by light of wavelength around 580 nm; one of the three primary colors in subtractive color systems.","The middle light in a set of three traffic lights, the lighting of which indicates that drivers should stop short of the intersection if it is safe to do so."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellow hue.","Lacking courage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow"},{"term":"submarine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Being, relating to, or made for use underwater, especially beneath the sea.","Hidden or undisclosed."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A boat that can go underwater.","Alternative form of submarine sandwich."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/submarine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Yellow Submarine (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Yellow Submarine\" is a song by the English rock band the Beatles from their 1966 album Revolver. It was also issued on a double A-side single, paired with \"Eleanor Rigby\". Written as a children's song by Paul McCartney and John Lennon, it was drummer Ringo Starr's vocal spot on the album. The single went to number one on charts in the United Kingdom and several other European countries, and in Australia, Canada and New Zealand. It won an Ivor Novello Award for the highest certified sales of any single written by a British songwriter and issued in the UK in 1966. In the US, the song peaked at number two on the Billboard Hot 100 chart."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/82/Eleanor_rigby_single_usa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow_Submarine_(song)"},{"title":"Yellow Submarine (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow Submarine is a 1968 animated musical film inspired by the music of the Beatles, directed by George Dunning with art direction by Heinz Edelmann. Initial press reports stated that the Beatles themselves would provide their own character voices. However, apart from composing and performing the songs, the real Beatles' only participation was in the closing scene of the film; the voices of their animated counterparts were provided by voice actors."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/6f/Beatles_Yellow_Submarine_move_poster.jpg/330px-Beatles_Yellow_Submarine_move_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow_Submarine_(film)"},{"title":"Submarine","blocks":[{"text":"A submarine is a watercraft capable of independent operation underwater. The term \"submarine\" is also sometimes used historically or informally to refer to remotely operated vehicles and robots, or to medium-sized or smaller vessels. Submarines are referred to as boats rather than ships regardless of their size."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/US_Navy_040730-N-1234E-002_PCU_Virginia_%28SSN_774%29_returns_to_the_General_Dynamics_Electric_Boat_shipyard.jpg/330px-US_Navy_040730-N-1234E-002_PCU_Virginia_%28SSN_774%29_returns_to_the_General_Dynamics_Electric_Boat_shipyard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Submarine"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/YellowSubTradeAd.jpg/500px-YellowSubTradeAd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/YellowSubTradeAd.jpg/500px-YellowSubTradeAd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Capitol Records ad for the \"Yellow Submarine\" / \"Eleanor Rigby\" single","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYellowSubTradeAd.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Student_Vietnam_War_protesters.JPG/500px-Student_Vietnam_War_protesters.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Student_Vietnam_War_protesters.JPG/500px-Student_Vietnam_War_protesters.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Anti-Vietnam War protestors at the University of Wisconsin–Madison. The song resonated with the student protest movement in the US.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStudent_Vietnam_War_protesters.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Nembutal_%28name-brand_pentobarbital%29%2C_100mg_capsules.jpg/500px-Nembutal_%28name-brand_pentobarbital%29%2C_100mg_capsules.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser